{"name":"Apple Brown Betty","hex":"#9c6757","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common, firm, round fruit produced by a tree of the genus Malus.","The fruit of the tree Malus domestica, chiefly with a green, red, or yellow skin, cultivated in temperate climates for cidermaking, cooking, and eating. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (something) appear like an apple (noun sense 1.1).","To become like an apple.\n\n To collect fir-cones.\n Of a flower bud or vegetable (especially a root vegetable): to grow into the shape of an apple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"},{"term":"betty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A short bar used by thieves to wrench doors open; a jimmy. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A picklock, skeleton key; a tool for opening locks."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pick a lock, to open with a betty.","To be overly attentive to someone or something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/betty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brown Betty (dessert)","blocks":[{"text":"A Brown Betty is a traditional American dessert made from fruit, usually apple, but also berries or pears and sweetened crumbs. Similar to a cobbler or apple crisp, the fruit is baked, and, in this case, the sweetened crumbs are placed in layers between the fruit. It is usually served with lemon sauce or whipped cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Brown_Betty_serving.jpg/330px-Brown_Betty_serving.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_Betty_(dessert)","wikidata":"Q4976066"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"},{"title":"Betty","blocks":[{"text":"Betty or Bettie is a feminine given name. It is commonly a diminutive for the names Bethany and Elizabeth. In Latin America, it is also a common diminutive for the given name Beatriz, the Spanish and Portuguese form of the Latin name Beatrix and the English name Beatrice. In the 17th and 18th centuries, it was more often a diminutive of Bethia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Betty","wikidata":"Q2090092"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Malus_domestica_a1.jpg/500px-Malus_domestica_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thu